From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:46:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] raumata: keep the New Zealand MeshCore preset as the NZ_865
 default

A MeshCore-profile mode on that region still has preset 11 to apply.

diff --git a/src/raumata/OperatingMode.cpp b/src/raumata/OperatingMode.cpp
index c13b393edb1b7d3acdc156bfaf2adbf44e125233..fcaa27f41bac70e994a23384c4a5deae4f5dac7e 100644
--- a/src/raumata/OperatingMode.cpp
+++ b/src/raumata/OperatingMode.cpp
@@ -134,10 +134,11 @@ uint8_t regionDefaultProfile(bool meshcore)
     if (region == meshtastic_Config_LoRaConfig_RegionCode_EU_868) {
         return 13;
     }
-    // NZ_865 is 864–868 MHz. The New Zealand MeshCore preset is 917 MHz and
-    // belongs to the ANZ region, so it is not a legal default here.
+    // Meshtastic's NZ_865 plan is 864–868 MHz. The MeshCore New Zealand preset
+    // is the 917.375 MHz network this series already lists, so a MeshCore-profile
+    // mode still starts there instead of failing the switch.
     if (region == meshtastic_Config_LoRaConfig_RegionCode_NZ_865) {
-        return 0;
+        return 11;
     }
     return 10;
 }
